-- title:
--   Integral closure in a Kummer extension F[X]/(X^k-vh^k)
-- statement:
--   Let $B$ be an integrally closed domain with a field of fractions $F$, realised by an algebra structure $B \to F$ making $F$ a fraction ring of $B$. Let $k$ be a natural number whose image in $B$ is a unit, let $v$ be a unit of $B$, and let $h \in F$ be nonzero. Let $g \in F$ be given by $g = v h^{k}$ (the image of $v$ under $B \to F$ times $h^{k}$), and form the $F$-algebra $L := F[X]/(X^{k} - g)$, written as `AdjoinRoot (X ^ k - C g)`, with distinguished element `AdjoinRoot.root` the class $\alpha$ of $X$. The conclusion is a conjunction of three assertions: first, the integral closure of $B$ in $L$ is exactly the $B$-subalgebra of $L$ generated by the single element $h^{-1}\alpha$, where $h^{-1}$ is transported to $L$ along $F \to L$; second, this integral closure is an étale $B$-algebra; third, it is a finite $B$-module. The $B$-algebra structure on $L$, and hence the meaning of the integral closure, is the one coming from $B \to F \to L$.
--
--   This is the affine-local description of the normalisation of a normal base in a Kummer extension obtained by extracting a $k$-th root of a unit times a $k$-th power, the point being that after the substitution $X \mapsto hX$ the algebra becomes the standard Kummer algebra $B[X]/(X^{k}-v)$, which is finite étale over $B$ when $k$ and $v$ are units. It is used in the scheme-theoretic form of the statement, for the existence and uniqueness of lifts from a normalisation along a Kummer covering over an affine open and for the finiteness and étaleness of that normalisation map.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_IsIntegrallyClosed_integralClosure_eq_adjoin_and_etale_and_finite_of_eq_mul_pow.lean

